      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since there isn\u0027t much commonality in this base class, I think it would be less intrusive to handle expression builders explicitly.  Something along these lines\n\n  bool AnimatablePropertyContainer::bindImpl(const AnimationBuilder\u0026 abuilder,\n                                             const skjson::ObjectValue* jprop,\n -                                           KeyframeAnimatorBuilder\u0026 builder) {\n +                                           KeyframeAnimatorBuilder\u0026 builder,\n +                                           ExpressionAnimatorBuilder* ebuilder) {\n      if (!jprop) {\n          return false;\n      }\n @@ -58,7 +59,14 @@ bool AnimatablePropertyContainer::bindImpl(const AnimationBuilder\u0026 abuilder,\n      const auto\u0026 jpropK \u003d (*jprop)[\"k\"];\n \n      if (!(*jprop)[\"x\"].is\u003cskjson::NullValue\u003e()) {\n -        abuilder.log(Logger::Level::kWarning, nullptr, \"Unsupported \nexpression.\");\n +        if (ebuilder) {\n +            if (auto eanimator \u003d ebuilder-\u003emake(abuilder, (*jprop)[\"x\"])) {\n +                fAnimators.push_back(std::move(eanimator));\n +                return true;\n +            }\n +        } else {\n +            abuilder.log(Logger::Level::kWarning, nullptr, \"Ignoring expression.\");\n +        }\n      }\n\nThen you don\u0027t have to touch the existing animators/builders and can pass the right type of expression builder from AnimatablePropertyContainer::bind\u003c\u003e specializations.  WDYT?",
      "revId": "b8dd21ea0b2330dd420dd3e39d8f862210d11c75",
